meta {
  name: Live Floor Map
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurant_id}}/floor-map
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Placed stations and storage locations sit on each area, like tables
  (guide v57 §93). areas[].stations and areas[].storage_locations carry
  area_id, pos_x, pos_y, width, height and status. Station status: state
  (idle, cooking, ready, late), pending, preparing, ready, orders,
  oldest_minutes. late = the oldest line still cooking was sent over 20
  minutes ago. Storage status: state (out, low, stocked, empty),
  in_stock, low_stock, out_of_stock. Counts are items, from stock_qty.
  empty means no item is kept there.
  Top-level stations and storage_locations list every one, placed or not
  (area_id null when not on the floor), with the same status.
  Elements are wall, door, host_area and entrance only. They have no
  station_id, storage_location_id, station_status or storage_status.
}
